<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint John River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saint John River flows from Maine through New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-fundy">Bay of Fundy</a>. About 14,000 Loyalists settled along it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>, leading to the creation of the Colony of New Brunswick in 1784, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fredericton">Fredericton</a> on the river as capital and the city of Saint John at its mouth.</p></div>
